From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tao Gong <gongtao0607@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: bypass HW_RRO for sub-64 window BlockAck sessions

Apple macOS/iOS stations negotiate sub-64 window BlockAck sessions on
latency-sensitive queues (such as TID 6 with buf_size = 8 and TID 1
with buf_size = 16) alongside standard bulk queues (TID 0 with
buf_size = 64/256).

The MT7996 HW_RRO (Hardware Receive Reordering Offload) engine is
architected around standard 64-frame minimum BlockAck bitmap windows.
Enabling HW_RRO (ba_rdd_rro = 1) on sub-64 window sessions causes
the MT7996 on-chip reordering ring and SRAM session lookup state machine
to enter an invalid state, stalling hardware RX offload on subsequent
associations reusing that WCID.

Bypass HW_RRO for RX BlockAck sessions with buf_size < 64, delegating
sub-64 window streams to standard mac80211 software reordering while
preserving full hardware offload acceleration for standard bulk data
streams (buf_size >= 64).

Signed-off-by: Tao Gong <gongtao0607@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -1752,7 +1752,8 @@ mt7996_mcu_sta_ba(struct mt7996_dev *dev
 	ba->ba_en = enable << params->tid;
 	ba->amsdu = params->amsdu;
 	ba->tid = params->tid;
-	ba->ba_rdd_rro = !tx && enable && mt7996_has_hwrro(dev);
+	ba->ba_rdd_rro = !tx && enable && mt7996_has_hwrro(dev) &&
+			 params->buf_size >= 64;
 
 	return mt76_mcu_skb_send_msg(&dev->mt76, skb,
 				     MCU_WMWA_UNI_CMD(STA_REC_UPDATE), true);
